{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.912,
            0.049,
            0.954,
            0.068
          ],
          "content": "161"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.083,
            0.677,
            0.107
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "11.6 Images Formed in a Plane Mirror"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.126,
            0.728,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "Look into the mirror. Do you see your face in it? What you see is a reflection of your face in the mirror. We also see reflections of other objects that are in front of the mirror. Let us try to find out more about this."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.208,
            0.453,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "**Activity 11.7: Let us experiment**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.244,
            0.656,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": "Take a plane mirror and a pen or some other object."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.267,
            0.661,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": "Place the pen in front of the mirror as shown in Fig. 11.10."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.308,
            0.662,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "What do you see in the mirror? It appears as if a similar pen is placed behind the mirror. The pen which appears behind the mirror is the **image** of the pen formed by the mirror. The pen itself is the **object**."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.673,
            0.202,
            0.879,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.677,
                0.338,
                0.869,
                0.37
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 11.10: Image of a pen in a plane mirror"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.383,
            0.728,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": "Now, move the pen to different positions in front of the mirror and **compare** the sizes of the images of the pen at each position."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.442,
            0.727,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "Are the two sizes the same? The image formed by a plane mirror is of the same size as the object."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.481,
            0.726,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": "Again, move the pen to different positions in front of the mirror and observe if the image is upright at each position."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.522,
            0.727,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "Does the tip of the pen appear on top at each position? An upright image is called **erect**. An image formed by a plane mirror is erect."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.578,
            0.727,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "Now, place a screen vertically behind the mirror. Move it around. Do you get the image on the screen? Repeat this by placing the screen in front of the mirror."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.637,
            0.722,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "The image formed by a plane mirror cannot be obtained on a screen."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.684,
            0.454,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": "**Activity 11.8: Let us experiment**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.865,
            0.983,
            0.952,
            0.995
          ],
          "content": "4/3/2025 4:56:34 PM"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.719,
            0.722,
            0.756
          ],
          "content": "Stand in front of a plane mirror and look at your image (Fig. 11.11). Notice how far it appears to be from the mirror."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.759,
            0.722,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "Now, stand close to the mirror. Is the image also closer to the mirror?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.797,
            0.723,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "Stand at different distances from the mirror and notice how far the image appears to be from the mirror in each case. Do you find any relation between your distance from the mirror and the distance of your image from the mirror?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.738,
            0.543,
            0.921,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "",
